clisp-plain-wrapper
===================

Wrap plain text files to be readable with a fixed width.

(Made before I realized fold exists.)

* wraps at 72 columns by default
* keeps blank lines, so paragraphs stay separated
* words longer than the width are left unbroken
* keeps each line's indentation on the lines wrapped from it
* measures width in display columns (wide characters count as two)

Usage
-----

	clisp src/wrap.lisp <file> [width]

Wrap a file at the default width:

	clisp src/wrap.lisp example

Wrap a file at 60 columns and save the result:

	clisp src/wrap.lisp example 60 > example.wrapped

Example output:

	Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Ut
	vitae mi ut turpis ultrices imperdiet a in ligula. Mauris
	nec auctor odio. Proin commodo urna at enim interdum
